# {{ project_name }}

A cross-platform Python UI project using
[Pydrud](https://github.com/MurShidM01/Pydrud) {{ pydrud_version }}.

This project uses the **Pydash** runtime by default. Python executes on the
host; a separately installed Pydash preview client connects over the
single-run authenticated LAN preview protocol. The client receives widget
trees and patches, never project source code. No Android SDK, NDK, Gradle,
adb, or embedded-Python build is part of this project.

The starter screen is **Heartbeat** — one calm screen with a softly pulsing
heart, a live BPM reading, a scrolling ECG trace and a compact transport
button. Open `src/app/screens/heartbeat.py` to shape the screen,
`src/app/theme.py` to re-brand it, or `src/app/theme.pss` to tune its visual
design.

## Run it

```bash
pydrud dev              # run Python locally and print a Pydash connection QR/URI
python -m pytest -q tests # run the project tests
pydrud analyze          # check the Python UI code
```

Use the matching preview client to scan the QR or enter the printed URI. Keep
the host and client on a trusted network; the pairing token is single-run and
is not encrypted by the preview transport. Do not expose the preview port to
the public internet.

